########################################################################################################################
# Help for command history
########################################################################################################################
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[CTRL + X THEN L] or  lc : re-run a previous command from your shell history
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reads bash's own history (the same list "history" shows), most recent first, deduplicated so a
repeated command only appears once (at its most recent position).

If fzf is installed (and NIXLPER_LAST_COMMAND_FUZZY is not disabled), opens an incremental
filter that supports BOTH styles at once — each entry is shown with its index number:
  - type digits (e.g. "3") to jump straight to that numbered entry, like the numbered list
  - type letters (e.g. "docker") to fuzzy-filter the list live by command text
Arrow keys to move, Enter to select, Esc to cancel.

Without fzf — or with NIXLPER_LAST_COMMAND_FUZZY=false — falls back to a numbered list:
type a number and press Enter to select it.

Either way, the selected command is NOT run blindly: it is preloaded onto an editable prompt
("Run> ") so you can review it, tweak it, or clear the line to cancel before pressing Enter.

Example output (numbered fallback):
   1) git status
   2) docker ps -a
   3) rm -rf build/
   Select [1-3] (Enter to cancel):
   Run> git status

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Configuration (via nconf or ~/.config/nixlper/nixlper.conf):

  NIXLPER_LAST_COMMAND_MAX     int    50      Maximum number of history entries considered
  NIXLPER_LAST_COMMAND_FUZZY   bool   true    Use fzf fuzzy filter when fzf is installed

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
